-- title:
--   Translation pull-back carries vanishing at 2S to S
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a field, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, and $K$ an algebraically closed field that is an $R$-algebra, such that the base-changed curve $W⁄K$ is elliptic and its affine coordinate ring $(W⁄K).\mathrm{CoordinateRing}$ is a Dedekind domain. Let $S$ be a point of the affine curve $W⁄K$ with $S \ne 0$ and $S + S \ne 0$, let $h$ be an element of the function field $(W⁄K).\mathrm{FunctionField}$ (the fraction field of the coordinate ring), and let $k$ be a natural number. For a nonzero point $P$, `placeOf W K P hP` denotes the height-one prime of the coordinate ring whose ideal is the one generated by the classes of $X - x(P)$ and $Y - y(P)$, which is maximal because the affine coordinates of $P$ give a nonsingular point, and nonzero because the class of $X - x(P)$ is nonzero. Writing $v_P$ for the associated adic valuation with values in $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$, and $\exp$ for the embedding of $\mathbb{Z}$ into that group, the hypothesis is $v_{S+S}(h) \le \exp(-k)$, i.e. $h$ vanishes to order at least $k$ at the place of $S+S$. The conclusion is $v_S\big(\tau_S^{*}h\big) \le \exp(-k)$, where $\tau_S^{*} =$ `transEquiv W K S` is the $K$-algebra automorphism of the function field given by the translation pull-back along $S$, with inverse the pull-back along $-S$.
--
--   This is the doubling case $P = S$ of the transport of adic valuations along the translation pull-back: pulling back by translation by $S$ moves the order of vanishing at $2S$ to an order of vanishing at least as large at $S$. It is used in the verification of the valuation-theoretic properties of the functions entering the Weil pairing, being cited by [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.valuation_transEquiv_weilFun`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.valuation_transEquiv_weilFun).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_Affine_valuation_transEquiv_le_self.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_EllipticCurve_FunctionFieldPullback

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine IsDedekindDomain WithZero

theorem WeierstrassCurve.Affine.valuation_transEquiv_le_self {R : Type*} [Field R] (W : WeierstrassCurve R) (K : Type*) [Field K] [Algebra R K] [DecidableEq K] [IsAlgClosed K] [W.IsElliptic] [IsDedekindDomain (W⁄K).CoordinateRing] {S : (W⁄K).Point} (hS : S ≠ 0) (h2S : S + S ≠ 0) (h : (W⁄K).FunctionField) (k : ℕ) (hh : (placeOf W K (S + S) h2S).valuation (W⁄K).FunctionField h ≤ exp (-(k : ℤ))) : (placeOf W K S hS).valuation (W⁄K).FunctionField (transEquiv W K S h) ≤ exp (-(k : ℤ)) := by sorry
